explanation:
The issue arises from the way the code handles null values within the array. When `array[i]` is null, calling `array[i].getClass()` results in a NullPointerException because `getClass()` cannot be called on null. To fix this, the code should check for null before attempting to call `getClass()` on each element of the array.

The corrected loop should include an additional condition to handle the case where `array[i]` is null:

for (int i = 0; i < array.length; i++) {
    if (array[i] != null) {
        classes[i] = array[i].getClass();
    } else {
        classes[i] = null;
    }
}
